      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Docs MCP Maintenance",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "40-guides/10-docs-mcp"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " contains the setup, skill-authoring, synchronization, and recovery procedures."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-2": {
      "id": "maintenance-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Process and Task Ownership"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-3": {
      "id": "maintenance-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Codex and Claude use stdio MCP bridges, and pi uses its extension bridge. They connect to one authenticated loopback daemon per state directory. The service resolves an explicit project to its canonical docs root and calls the existing store through typed tools. No model or kernel process is started by an external documentation task."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-4": {
      "id": "maintenance-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The service owns workspace membership and in-memory task state. Store operations own structural validation, revision checks, and root-scoped mutation coordination. Task IDs are bound to the workspace. Each task pins a guidance snapshot, records whether it has read the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "style",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " topic, and keeps one edit baseline per page, without creating a transaction. Direct valid edits persist immediately. The shared workbench proxies to this same daemon. Standalone workbenches and kernel processes retain independent process-local state."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-5": {
      "id": "maintenance-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Maintained and Derived Files"
